tor] okay and how high is your blood pressure been running\n[patient] it\'s been running over one fifty\n[doctor] okay and have you noticed any other symptoms with that like chest pain or shortness of breath\n[patient] no i haven\'t had any of that\n[doctor] alright and how about headaches have you been having any headaches\n[patient] yeah i\'ve had some headaches but i\'m not sure if it\'s from stress at work or my blood pressure\n[doctor] okay and have you noticed any swelling in your legs or feet\n[patient] no i haven\'t noticed any of that\n[doctor] okay and have you been exercising regularly\n[patient] i\'ve been trying to but i haven\'t been able to do as much as i would like\n[doctor] alright and have you been eating healthy\n[patient] i\'ve been trying to eat healthy but i\'ve been stressed out with work and that\'s been making it hard\n[doctor] okay so what kind of work do you do\n[patient] i\'m a nurse practitioner\n[doctor] okay that\'s great i\'m glad you\'re in the medical field but it sounds like it\'s been pretty stressful\n[patient] yeah it has been really stressful\n[doctor] alright so let\'s go ahead and check your blood pressure today and i\'m also gon na do a quick physical exam and then we\'ll talk about some treatment options\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] so your blood pressure today is one forty over ninety and that is a little bit higher than what we would like to see so i\'m gon na go ahead and order a lipid panel and a metabolic panel and we\'ll check your kidney function to make sure everything is looking good with that kidney transplant that you had a few years ago\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] and i\'m gon na start you on carvedilol twenty five milligrams twice a day and that will help bring your blood pressure down a little bit\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] and i know you mentioned that you\'ve been trying to eat healthy but let\'s talk a little bit about diet and lifestyle changes\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] so i know you\'re a nurse practitioner and you\'re probably familiar with the importance of diet and lifestyle changes but it\'s really important to make sure you\'re eating a diet that is low in salt and low in fat and high in fiber and also to make sure you\'re staying hydrated\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] and have you been exercising regularly\n[patient] i\'ve been trying to but like i said i haven\'t been able to do as much as i would like\n[doctor] okay well let\'s talk a little bit about that and let\'s set a goal for you to try to exercise at least thirty minutes a day five days a week\n[patient] okay that sounds good\n[doctor] and i\'m gon na go ahead and prescribe you some carvedilol twenty five milligrams twice a day and we\'ll see how that works for you\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] and i\'m gon na order a lipid panel and a metabolic panel and we\'ll check your kidney function and we\'ll go from there\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] and do you have any other questions for me\n[patient] no that\'s it\n[doctor] okay well i\'m glad to see you and i\'ll see you back in a few weeks\n[patient] thank you }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi, susan.\n[patient] hi.\n[doctor] how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing well, thank you.\n[doctor] so, i know that you\'ve been having some high blood pressure. is that correct?\n[patient] yes, i have high blood pressure.\n[doctor] okay. and when was that diagnosed?\n[patient] it\'s been a long time. i don\'t remember.\n[doctor] okay.\n[patient] i\'ve always had high blood pressure.\n[doctor] okay. and is it out of control?\n[patient] it seems out of control.\n[doctor] okay. have you been taking any medications for it?\n[patient] i\'ve been taking norvasc ten milligrams daily.\n[doctor] okay. and is that helping?\n[patient] i\'m not sure.\n[doctor] okay. have you been checking your blood pressure at home?\n[patient] yes.\n[doctor] okay. and what\'s been your blood pressure?\n[patient] it\'s been over one fifty.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any chest pain or shortness o