patient will be given a glucometer to monitor her glucose levels at home.\n\nAtrial Fibrillation.\n\n• Medical Reasoning: Asymptomatic and well-controlled at this time.\n• Medical Treatment: Continue metoprolol 25 mg twice daily. Refilled today.\n\nHistory of Reflux.\n\n• Medical Reasoning: Well-controlled on current regimen.\n• Medical Treatment: Continue Protonix 40 mg daily.\n\nPatient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] hi, how are you doing today?\n\n[patient] i\'m doing okay, i just came in because i\'ve been having some issues with my blood sugar.\n\n[doctor] okay, well, let\'s go ahead and go through everything. so, you\'ve been having some issues with your blood sugar. what\'s been going on?\n\n[patient] so, i was at my family\'s house over the holidays and i think i just ate too much. i mean, i\'ve been eating a lot of sweets and i\'ve been feeling really lightheaded and dizzy.\n\n[doctor] okay. and how long have you been feeling lightheaded and dizzy?\n\n[patient] it\'s been this past week.\n\n[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any other symptoms like seeing spots in your vision or anything like that?\n\n[patient] yeah, i\'ve been seeing spots in my vision and i\'ve been feeling really dizzy.\n\n[doctor] okay. and did you have any fever or chills?\n\n[patient] no, i didn\'t have a fever or chills.\n\n[doctor] okay. and any chest pain or shortness of breath?\n\n[patient] no, none of that.\n\n[doctor] okay. and any abdominal pain or burning when you urinate?\n\n[patient] no, none of that either.\n\n[doctor] okay. and any joint pain or muscle aches?\n\n[patient] no, nothing seems out of the ordinary for my joint pain.\n\n[doctor] okay. so, you have a history of osteoarthritis. is there anything out of the ordinary for that?\n\n[patient] no, nothing seems out of the ordinary for my joint pain.\n\n[doctor] okay. and you also have a history