kely will be the time of her second naltrexone injection.\n\nRecommend upgrading influenza vaccination and Shingrix #2, she defers this.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nCall the clinic with any questions. Make follow up appointment week of June 14th.\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] hi, amanda, how are you?\n[patient] hi, doctor. i\'m doing okay.\n[doctor] good to see you. how have you been?\n[patient] i\'ve been doing well. just trying to manage my blood pressure.\n[doctor] alright. so i see that you\'re here for a follow-up. you were here last time for hypertension and alcohol use disorder. what\'s going on?\n[patient] yes, i\'ve been managing my blood pressure. it\'s been a little bit higher.\n[doctor] okay. so, at your last visit on april 16th, your blood pressure was 130 over 90. and then you presented at 150 over 100. we put you on hydrochlorothiazide 12.5 milligrams once daily and lisinopril 20 milligrams once daily. and how are you doing on that?\n[patient] i\'ve been taking the medication, but my blood pressure is still a little high.\n[doctor] okay. well, your cmp and cbc were essentially unremarkable. have you been checking your blood pressure?\n[patient] yes, i\'ve been checking it in the morning and evening. it\'s a little higher in the evening.\n[doctor] okay. and what\'s your blood pressure been?\n[patient] it\'s been averaging 135 to 145 over 95 to 110.\n[doctor] okay. have you noticed any side effects from the lisinopril?\n[patient] yes, i\'ve had some headaches and this feeling like my ear is filled with water.\n[doctor] okay. and how have you been doing with that?\n[patient] i took half a dose and i didn\'t have the side effects.\n[doctor] okay. and how about the hydrochlorothiazide?\n[patient] i\'ve been taking that.\n[doctor] okay. have you noticed any side effects from that?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t.\n[doctor] okay. do you have any other questions about your medications?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] alright. so, i know you\'ve 