discharge last week. She notes that this did not alarm her until the right side of her vagina became painful and sore, which has not subsided. She states that she had an abnormal Pap Smear around the age of 20, but all her Pap Smears since then, including her most recent one approximately 6 months ago, have all been normal.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM\n\nGenitourinary\nPelvic exam: No external lesions, normal labia majora and labia minora. Normal physiological discharge with normal color and odor. Cervix is normal, vaginal wall is normal, no cervical motion tenderness or masses noted. Swabs were obtained for sexual transmitted disease testing.\n\nASSESSMENT\n\n• Screening for sexually transmitted disease.\n\nPLAN\n\nMs. Ross is a 23-year-old female who presents today as a new patient for full-spectrum STD testing. We will screen her today for gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, syphilis, HIV, and hepatitis C. Patient is high risk due to an abnormal pap smear in the past and the recent discovery of her sexual partner having multiple partners for some period of time. We will call the patient with the results of the laboratory testing.\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] good afternoon, how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing okay, i just need to get some tests done.\n[doctor] alright, i\'m doctor martin. i understand that you\'re here for full-spectrum std testing. what seems to be the reason for that?\n[patient] yeah, so i\'ve been having some symptoms and i\'m just really worried about getting something.\n[doctor] okay. so, what kind of symptoms are you experiencing?\n[patient] um, discomfort, a change in my discharge, and a bad odor in my vaginal area.\n[doctor] mm-hmm. and how long have you been noticing these symptoms?\n[patient] it started about a week ago.\n[doctor] okay. and have you noticed anything else? like a fever or chills?\n[patient] no, no fever or chills.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any pain in your lower abdomen or pelvis?\n[patient] yes, the right side of my vagina is getting really painful and sore.\n[doctor] okay. have you noticed any changes in your discharge?\n[patient] yeah, the color and the consistency is different.\n[doctor] okay. and when you say the color and the consistency is different, what do you mean?\n[patient] it\'s not normal. it\'s like it\'s thicker and it smells bad.\n[doctor] okay. and how long have you been with your current partner?\n[patient] we\'ve been together for about three years.\n[doctor] okay. and do you know if they\'ve been with other people?\n[patient] no, i just found out.\n[doctor] okay. and did you find out recently?\n[patient] yeah, recently. they told me.\n[doctor] okay. and how did you find out?\n[patient] they told me.\n[doctor] okay. and how have you been feeling about this?\n[patient] i\'m really upset and worried.\n[doctor] yeah, i can imagine. so, have you talked to them about it?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t.\n[doctor] okay. and have you talked to anyone else about it?\n[patient] no, i just came here.\n[doctor] okay. alright. well, i\'m glad you\'re here. so, let\'s go ahead and do a quick exam. i\'m just gon na do a pelvic exam. it\'s very quick and it\'s painless. i\'m gon na just feel your abdomen and then i\'m gon na look at your vagina. i\'m just gon na check for any lesions or abnormalities. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] alright, i\'m gon na just check your abdomen now. everything looks normal. i\'m gon na check your vagina now. everything looks normal. i\'m gon na check your cervix now. everything looks normal. your vaginal walls look normal. i don\'t see any cervical motion tenderness or any masses. i\'m gon na get some swabs now to test for stds. we\'re gon na check for gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, syphilis, hiv, and hepatitis c. i know it\'s a lot, but we\'re gon na do all of them to make sure we catch everything. i know it\'s a lot to take in, but i\'ll be here to support you every step of the way. do you have any questions about the testing?\n[patient] no, i think you covered everything.\n[doctor] okay. great. we\'ll call you when we get the results. i\'ll have my nurse come in and we\'ll get you checked out. sound good?\n[patient] yeah, that\'s fine.\n[doctor] alright. i\'m gon na go ahead and order the tests and we\'ll call you when we get the results. do you have any other questions?\n[patient] no, that\'s all.\n[doctor] okay. great. my nurse will be in shortly. do you have any other medical issues or concerns that we should know about?\n[patient] no, i don\'t think so.\n[doctor] okay. great. my nurse will be in shortly to get you checked out. do you have a primary care doctor?\n[patient] i don\'t think so.\n[doctor] okay. great. we\'ll get you set up with one if you need it. my nurse will be in shortly. thank you for coming in today.\n[patient] thank you.\n[doctor] okay. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] good morning\n[patient] good morning\n[doctor] hey, um, good morning, so, i\'m doctor smith, i\'m one of the physicians here at the urgent care center. i\'m here to do a full spectrum std test. i know it\'s a little bit uncomfortable, but it\'s really important to do this, so let\'s get started. how are you doing?\n[patient] i\'m doing well\n[doctor] good, good, so, um, tell me a little bit about what\'s going on. what\'s going on with your symptoms?\n[patient] um, i\'ve been having some discomfort and a change in my discharge, and i\'ve noticed that the right side of my vagina is starting to get a little bit painful.\n[doctor] okay, and, um, is that a new onset of symptoms? or has that been going on for a while?\n[patient] it\'s been going on for about a week.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, have you noticed any fever or chills?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any odor?\n[patient] yes, i\'ve noticed a change in the odor, the color and the consistency of my discharge.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, how would you describe the odor? is it a normal, um, odor? or is i