re clear bilaterally. and on your neurological exam, your neurological exam is otherwise normal. and on your neck exam, you have no jugular venous distension or carotid bruits. all right. so let\'s talk a little bit about the results. so your most recent creatinine level is stable. and that\'s good. and on your hemoglobin a1c, it was 16. and that\'s a little high. we\'ll get that down. and i\'m going to order a repeat hemoglobin a1c. and we\'ll check that out. and i\'m going to refer you to a dietitian for some diabetes education. and we\'ll get that set up. and we\'ll also contact your primary care physician to see if we can get you on a more appropriate insulin regimen. all right. so let\'s talk a little bit about the plan. so i\'m going to prescribe you a refill of metoprolol 50 milligrams once a day. i\'m also going to prescribe you a refill of crestor 40 milligrams once a day. and i\'m going to continue you on brilinta for the next six months. and i\'m also going to refer you to cardiac rehab. and we\'ll get that set up. and we\'ll also get you set up with a dietitian for some diabetes education. and we\'ll get that set up. and we\'ll also contact your primary care physician to see if we can get you on a more appropriate insulin regimen. and i\'m also going to refer you to psychiatry. and we\'ll get that set up. all right. so i\'m going to go ahead and order all of those prescriptions and get those set up. and i\'m going to go ahead and order that repeat hemoglobin a1c and get that set up. and we\'ll get that set up. all right. so any questions?\n[patient] no, that\'s it.\n[doctor] okay. all right. well, i\'ll go ahead and get all of those set up. and we\'ll get you scheduled with the dietitian and the psychiatrist. and we\'ll get that set up. all right. well, i\'ll see you next time. thank you.\n[patient] thank you.\n[doctor] bye-bye.\n[patient] bye-bye. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Reference Answer:\n[doctor] hey jose how are you doing it\'s been about you know three o