kay. and any bruising?\n[patient] yeah, there\'s a little bit of bruising.\n[doctor] okay. any numbness or tingling?\n[patient] no, no numbness or tingling.\n[doctor] okay. all right. i\'m gon na go ahead and do a physical exam on you. so, i\'m gon na press on your elbow here. does that hurt?\n[patient] yeah, it hurts a little bit.\n[doctor] okay. okay. let me do a little bit of flexion and extension. is that okay?\n[patient] yeah.\n[doctor] okay. any pain with that?\n[patient] a little bit.\n[doctor] okay. and any pain with extension?\n[patient] a little bit.\n[doctor] okay. okay. let me check your vitals. your blood pressure is a little high today. 150 over 90. is that something that you\'ve noticed before?\n[patient] yeah, i have noticed that sometimes.\n[doctor] okay. all right. and i\'m gon na go ahead and check your heart. you have a systolic ejection murmur. but that\'s not something that i\'m really concerned about today. and your lungs are clear. let me go ahead and look at your x-ray. everything looks good. no fracture or any bony abnormalities. so, let\'s talk a little bit about what happened. you mentioned that your son hit you with a lacrosse stick. is that something that you\'ve done before?\n[patient] yeah, i\'ve played lacrosse before.\n[doctor] okay. and how often do you play?\n[patient] not too much. just occasionally.\n[doctor] okay. okay. so, let\'s talk a little bit about your symptoms. you said you have some pain. does it hurt to move your elbow?\n[patient] yeah, it hurts a little bit when i move it.\n[doctor] okay. any pain when you straighten it?\n[patient] a little bit.\n[doctor] okay. and when you bend it?\n[patient] a little bit.\n[doctor] okay. and any pain when you push on the back of your elbow?\n[patient] yeah, it hurts a little bit.\n[doctor] okay. okay. so, let\'s talk a little bit about your other medical conditions. you have hypertension. how are you managing that?\n[patient] i\'m managing it with diet and i take lisinopril.\n[doctor] okay. and how about your diabetes?\n[patient] i\'m managing that with metformin.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any other symptoms like increased thirst or urination?\n[patient] no, i don\'t have any other symptoms.\n[doctor] okay. all right. so, let\'s talk a little bit about your plan. i\'m gon na go ahead and prescribe you some ibuprofen. you can take 800 milligrams twice a day. that should help with some of the pain and swelling. you can also ice the area in 20-minute intervals three times a day. i think that should help a lot. and let\'s keep you on your lisinopril 20 milligrams a day. i think that\'s doing a good job with your hypertension. and let\'s keep you on your metformin 500 milligrams. we\'ll order a hemoglobin a1c to check how you\'re doing with your diabetes. and let\'s avoid playing lacrosse for the next couple of weeks. just until your elbow heals. after that, you should be fine to continue playing normally. does that sound okay?\n[patient] that sounds good.\n[doctor] okay. do you have any other questions?\n[patient] no, i think that\'s it.\n[doctor] okay. all right. i\'m gon na go ahead and order the hemoglobin a1c and we\'ll get that drawn today. and i\'ll have the nurse come in and get you checked out. and if you have any other questions or concerns, feel free to call me. okay?\n[patient] okay, thank you.\n[doctor] you\'re welcome. take care. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] good morning, how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing well, thank you.\n[doctor] good, good. um, i\'m doctor lee, i\'m one of the doctors at one medical group. it\'s nice to meet you. how can i help you today?\n[patient] i\'m doing well. i was wondering if i could get a quick appointment to get my blood pressure checked.\n[doctor] sure thing. i\'d be happy to check your blood pressure. um, so you said you\'re having a little bit of a problem with your elbow. tell me more about that.\n[patient] yeah, so i was playing lacrosse with my son over the weekend and he acc