lly high.\n[doctor] okay. so, they were able to get it under control?\n[patient] yeah, they did.\n[doctor] okay. and what about your ankles? you said your ankles were swollen?\n[patient] yeah, they were swollen.\n[doctor] okay. and was that because of the heart problem or was it something else?\n[patient] i\'m not sure.\n[doctor] okay. so, they did some tests and they said that your heart was functioning at about 55%. is that what they said?\n[patient] yeah, that\'s what they said.\n[doctor] okay. and did they say what was causing that?\n[patient] they said it was because of the fluid in my heart.\n[doctor] okay. and they said that you had some fluid in your heart?\n[patient] yeah, they said i had some fluid in my heart.\n[doctor] okay. and was that causing the heart failure?\n[patient] yeah, that was causing the heart failure.\n[doctor] okay. so, they were able to treat that?\n[patient] yeah, they were able to treat it.\n[doctor] okay. and are you still having any symptoms?\n[patient] yeah, i\'m still having some symptoms.\n[doctor] okay. what kind of symptoms?\n[patient] my ankles are still swollen.\n[doctor] okay. and are you having any chest pain?\n[patient] no, i\'m not having any chest pain.\n[doctor] okay. and are you having any shortness of breath?\n[patient] no, i\'m not having any shortness of breath.\n[doctor] okay. and are you having any other symptoms?\n[patient] no, i\'m just having some swelling in my ankles.\n[doctor] okay. so, what do you think caused this heart failure?\n[patient] i think it was because i was eating too much salt and my blood pressure was high.\n[doctor] okay. so, you think that was the cause?\n[patient] yeah, i think so.\n[doctor] okay. well, let\'s talk a little bit about your diet. have you been eating a lot of salty foods?\n[patient] yeah, i have been eating a lot of salty foods.\n[doctor] okay. and how much salt are you eating?\n[patient] i\'m not sure.\n[doctor] okay. do you have any idea?\n[patient] not really.\n[doctor] okay. well, we need to work on that. so, i\'m going to tell you what i\'m going to do. i\'m going to order a dietitian to come in and see you. she\'s going to help you with your diet. we need to get you to stop eating so much salt.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. and we\'re also going to get you to weigh yourself every day. if you gain 3 pounds in 2 days, you need to call me.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. so, let\'s talk a little bit about your blood pressure. have you been monitoring it at home?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t been monitoring it at home.\n[doctor] okay. so, when you were in the hospital, they were monitoring it, and it was high. so, we need to get that under control. i\'m going to put you back on the cozaar and norvasc. and i\'m also going to order a renal artery ultrasound. i want to check your kidney function.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. and i\'m also going to put you back on the bumex. and i want you to continue taking that. do you have any questions?\n[patient] no, i think that\'s it.\n[doctor] okay. and i\'ll see you in 3 months. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. take care. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi there, how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing good.\n[doctor] good. um, i know you had a recent hospital stay. i understand that you were in the hospital for a heart problem. can you tell me a little bit about what happened?\n[patient] yeah. i was in the hospital for a couple of days. i had a heart failure, um, exacerbation.\n[doctor] okay. and how are you feeling now?\n[patient] i\'m doing okay. i\'m still a little short of breath.\n[doctor] okay. and how about your swelling in your legs?\n[patient] i\'m a little bit swollen, but i\'m watching it.\n[doctor] okay. um, so i\'m going to go ahead and review your medical history. i see that you have a history of high blood pressure and stage three kidney disease. is that correct?\n[patient] that\'s correct.\n[doctor] okay. and any other medical problems?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] o